---
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { ownershipStandards, processSteps } from '../data/site';
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { withBasePath } from '../utils/helpers';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="About CHICAGOS #1 MSP | Chicago Technology Firm"
  description="An integrated Chicago technology firm connecting advisory, software engineering, cloud, cybersecurity, and managed operations."
>
  <PageHero
    title="We take the whole system personally."
    copy="Advice should survive delivery. Software should survive launch. Security should survive contact with daily work. Operations should keep improving instead of accumulating excuses."
    secondaryLabel="See the service model"
    secondaryHref="services/"
    asideTitle="Why the model is integrated"
    asideCopy="The largest technology firms connect consulting, engineering, security, and operations. We apply that logic at a tighter Chicago scale with a clearer line of accountability."
  />

  <section class="section story-section">
    <div class="shell story-section__grid">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>The handoff is where good work breaks.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="story-section__copy">
        <p>
          A roadmap can be sound and still fail in delivery. A software team can
          ship and still leave production unowned. A managed provider can keep
          tickets moving while the systems underneath the business keep
          drifting.
        </p>
        <p>
          CHICAGOS #1 MSP is built around the missing connection: one operating
          model that can carry a business decision into architecture, software,
          cloud, security, launch, support, and the next improvement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ownership-band">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>The standard behind the name.</h2>
      <ol>
        {
          ownershipStandards.map((item, index) => (
            <li>
              <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <strong>{item}</strong>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section principles-section">
    <div class="shell split-section split-section--top">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>How we make decisions.</h2>
        <p>Four rules keep broad capability from becoming vague delivery.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-list">
        <article>
          <span>01</span><h3>Name the outcome.</h3><p>
            Every engagement starts with the business decision, workflow,
            system, risk, or operating result it must change.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span><h3>Write the assumptions.</h3><p>
            We separate known facts, technical judgment, dependencies, and the
            choices the client still needs to make.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span><h3>Design for ownership.</h3><p>
            Access, source, data, documentation, recovery, support, and the exit
            path are parts of the system—not cleanup after the project.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span><h3>Operate what we recommend.</h3><p>
            Advice improves when the same operating model has to build, secure,
            support, and explain the result in production.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="delivery-band">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="delivery-band__heading">
        <h2>Plan it. Build it. Secure it. Run it.</h2>
        <p>Four stages, one accountable line of sight.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="delivery-band__steps">
        {
          processSteps.map(step => (
            <li>
              <span>{step.number}</span>
              <h3>{step.title}</h3>
              <p>{step.detail}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section local-section">
    <div class="shell local-section__inner">
      <h2>Chicago is the operating context.</h2>
      <p>
        We are built for established organizations across Chicago and the
        surrounding area that want senior access, practical on-site
        coordination, and a technology partner able to own both the build and
        the day-to-day reality around it.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={withBasePath('chicago/')}>
        Explore Chicago technology services <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</MarketingLayout>
